{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TransferMatrixLevelIndependence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TransferMatrixLevelIndependence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.transfer_matrix_level_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.transfer_matrix_level_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L187-L194","doc":"**Conditional on `conj:crystal-graph-realization`.** The canonical\nnormal form is annihilated by the composite of any two Kashiwara\nraising operators: `ẽ_i (ẽ_j · T_w) = 0` for all `i, j`. Derived\nfrom the highest-weight field (each factor is already `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.CrystalGraphRealization.highest_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.CrystalGraphRealization.highest_weight","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L184-L184","doc":"The canonical normal form is a crystal highest-weight vector:\nevery Kashiwara raising operator annihilates it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.CrystalGraphRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.CrystalGraphRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L181-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.CrystalGraphRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TransferMatrixLevel.ConditionalAudit.CrystalGraphRealization","kind":"class","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L168-L185","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:crystal-graph-realization`.\n\nUnder the Brundan–Kleshchev isomorphism, the Gröbner–Shirshov\ncanonical basis element `T_w ∈ H_n(R, q)` corresponds to a\nhighest-weight vector of the Kashiwara crystal\n`Cryst(𝔰𝔩_n)`: every Kashiwara raising operator `ẽ_i` annihilates\nit, `ẽ_i · T_w = 0`.\n\nConcrete content (shape of the claim): a Kashiwara-raising\nevaluator `raise : ℕ → ℤ` (indexed by simple root `i`) applied to\nthe canonical word that returns `0` on every index — the algebraic\nhighest-weight signature. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.transfer_matrix_level_independence_of_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.transfer_matrix_level_independence_of_derived","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**Level independence, in the form that is true.**  Configurations\nwith the same constituents have the same composite: the composite\ndepends on the constituent knots and on nothing else. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:transfer-matrix-level-independence","label":"prop:transfer-matrix-level-independence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedComposite.composite_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedComposite.composite_eq","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L130-L130","doc":"It is the Markov-trace product of the constituents -- the content\nthe free `compositePolynomial` field discarded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedComposite.composite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedComposite.composite","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The composite invariant of a configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedComposite.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedComposite.mk","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedComposite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedComposite","kind":"structure","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L124-L130","doc":"A composite invariant **derived from** the constituent list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.not_transfer_matrix_level_independence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.not_transfer_matrix_level_independence","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L107-L114","doc":"**`transfer_matrix_level_independence_axiom` is false**: the empty\nconfiguration has constituent product `1` and composite `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.emptyHadron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.emptyHadron","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L100-L105","doc":"A configuration with no constituents and zero composite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronConfig.constituents_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronConfig.constituents_length","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Correct number of constituents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronConfig.compositePolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronConfig.compositePolynomial","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The composite knot Skein polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronConfig.constituentPolynomials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronConfig.constituentPolynomials","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Constituent Skein polynomials (one per knot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronConfig.numConstituents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronConfig.numConstituents","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Number of constituent knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronConfig.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronConfig.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronConfig","kind":"structure","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L37-L46","doc":"A hadron configuration: constituent knots linked at a brane point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-level-independence.lean#L31-L33","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}